From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: An erase pass leaves the windows of other threads to themselves.

RDW_ERASENOW over windows of another thread (InvalidateRect( NULL ) does
it for every window of the system) sent each of them WM_NCPAINT and
WM_ERASEBKGND from the calling thread. The other thread took them one at a
time, with its own WM_PAINT in between: the background was erased after
the window had painted, and stayed. Windows erases only the windows of the
calling thread; the others erase when they paint.
---
diff --git a/server/window.c b/server/window.c
index 73ccd66..bcf693d 100644
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -1805,6 +1805,18 @@ static unsigned int get_update_flags( struct window *win, unsigned int flags )
 {
     unsigned int ret = 0;
 
+    /* Arctic: a pass that only erases (RDW_ERASENOW, InvalidateRect( NULL ),
+     * a window moved or hidden) is for the windows of the thread that makes
+     * it, as in Windows. The frame and the background of another thread's
+     * window were sent to it as two messages, each when it next took its
+     * messages, and it painted between them: the background came last, over
+     * what the window had just drawn, and nothing painted it again (the
+     * taskbar lost its icons that way). Such a window erases itself when it
+     * paints. */
+    if (!(flags & (UPDATE_PAINT | UPDATE_INTERNALPAINT)) && win->thread != current &&
+        !is_desktop_window( win ))  /* which never paints: whoever invalidates it erases it */
+        return 0;
+
     if (flags & UPDATE_NONCLIENT)
     {
         if ((win->paint_flags & PAINT_NONCLIENT) && win->update_region) ret |= UPDATE_NONCLIENT;
